.TH TAR 1 "2026-05-22" "hako" "hako utilities"
.SH NAME
tar \- list or extract tar archives
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tar
.B \-tf
.I archive
.br
.B tar
.B \-xf
.I archive
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tar
reads a tar archive and either lists its contents or extracts them into the
current directory.
.PP
Both ustar and pax extended archives are supported.
Sparse entries and archive creation are not supported.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-tf
List the paths of all entries in
.I archive
to standard output, one per line.
.TP
.B \-xf
Extract all entries from
.I archive
into the current directory.
Intermediate directories are created as needed.
.SH SECURITY
Path traversal is rejected: any entry whose path contains
.BR ..
or an absolute component causes an error and extraction stops immediately.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B "tar -tf archive.tar"
Print the contents of
.BR archive.tar .
.TP
.B "tar -xf archive.tar"
Extract
.B archive.tar
into the current directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Wrong arguments, unreadable archive, truncated data, unsupported entry type,
or a path traversal attempt.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tar (1),
.BR hako (1)
